{"id":"mahabharata-12-335","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":335,"title":"पञ्चत्रिंशदधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 335 · Janamejaya asks what Vyasa told","summary":{"en":"Janamejaya asks for the account of the Lord's greatness, his birth in the house of Dharma as Nara and Narayana, the boar's creation and the origin of the rice balls. Vyasa tells Yudhishthira how the Vedas were stolen by two demons, and how Brahma, left in darkness, praised the Lord who slept on the waters.","kn":"ಭಗವಂತನ ಮಹಿಮೆ, ಧರ್ಮನ ಮನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ನರ-ನಾರಾಯಣರಾಗಿ ಜನ್ಮ, ವರಾಹ ಸೃಷ್ಟಿ, ಪಿಂಡೋತ್ಪತ್ತಿಯ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಜನಮೇಜಯ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಬ್ಬರು ದಾನವರು ವೇದಗಳನ್ನು ಕದ್ದುದು, ಕತ್ತಲಲ್ಲಿದ್ದ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ನೀರಿನ ಮೇಲೆ ಮಲಗಿದ ಭಗವಂತನನ್ನು ಸ್ತುತಿಸಿದುದನ್ನು ವ್ಯಾಸ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जनमेजय भगवान की महिमा, धर्म के घर में नर-नारायण के रूप में जन्म, वराह की रचना और पिण्डों की उत्पत्ति पूछते हैं। व्यास युधिष्ठिर को बताते हैं कि दो दानव वेद चुरा ले गए और अन्धकार में पड़े ब्रह्मा ने जल पर सोए भगवान की स्तुति की।","te":"భగవంతుని మహిమ, ధర్ముని ఇంట నర నారాయణులుగా జన్మ, వరాహ సృష్టి, పిండోత్పత్తి గురించి జనమేజయుడు అడుగుతాడు. ఇద్దరు రాక్షసులు వేదాలను అపహరించారని, చీకటిలో ఉన్న బ్రహ్మ నీటిపై నిద్రించిన భగవంతుని స్తుతించాడని వ్యాసుడు యుధిష్ఠిరునికి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"இறைவனின் பெருமை, தர்மனின் இல்லத்தில் நர நாராயணராகப் பிறப்பு, வராகப் படைப்பு, பிண்டங்களின் தோற்றம் பற்றி ஜனமேஜயன் கேட்கிறான். இரு அசுரர் வேதங்களைத் திருடினர், இருளில் இருந்த பிரம்மன் நீரில் துயிலும் இறைவனைப் புகழ்ந்தான் என்று வியாசர் யுதிஷ்டிரனுக்குக் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ഭഗവാന്റെ മഹത്ത്വം, ധർമ്മന്റെ ഗൃഹത്തിൽ നരനും നാരായണനുമായുള്ള ജനനം, വരാഹത്തിന്റെ സൃഷ്ടി, അരിയുരുളകളുടെ ഉത്ഭവം എന്നിവ ജനമേജയൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. രണ്ടു അസുരന്മാർ വേദങ്ങളെ മോഷ്ടിച്ചതും, ജലത്തിൽ ഉറങ്ങുന്ന ഭഗവാനെ ഇരുട്ടിൽ അവശേഷിച്ച ബ്രഹ്മാവ് സ്തുതിച്ചതും വ്യാസൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനോട് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.335; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"श्रुतं भगवतस्तस्य माहात्म्यं परमात्मनः ।\nजन्म धर्मगृहे चैव नरनारायणात्मकम् ।\nमहावराहसृष्टा च पिण्डोत्पत्तिः पुरातनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have heard the greatness of that blessed Supreme Self, his birth in Dharma's house as Nara and Narayana, and the ancient origin of the pinda balls made by the great Boar."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रवृत्तौ च निवृत्तौ च यो यथा परिकल्पितः ।\nस तथा नः श्रुतो ब्रह्मन्कथ्यमानस्त्वयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, sinless one, as you told it, I have heard how the paths of action and of renunciation were each arranged."}},{"n":3,"text":"यच्च तत्कथितं पूर्वं त्वया हयशिरो महत् ।\nहव्यकव्यभुजो विष्णोरुदक्पूर्वे महोदधौ ।\nतच्च दृष्टं भगवता ब्रह्मणा परमेष्ठिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the great Horse-head you spoke of earlier, of Vishnu the enjoyer of offerings to gods and ancestors, in the great ocean to the north-east, was also seen by the blessed Brahma, Parameshthin."}},{"n":4,"text":"किं तदुत्पादितं पूर्वं हरिणा लोकधारिणा ।\nरूपं प्रभावमहतामपूर्वं धीमतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the wise, what was that form, never before seen and of great power, that Hari, the upholder of the worlds, had earlier produced?"}},{"n":5,"text":"दृष्ट्वा हि विबुधश्रेष्ठमपूर्वममितौजसम् ।\nतदश्वशिरसं पुण्यं ब्रह्मा किमकरोन्मुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sage, seeing that unprecedented, holy, immeasurably mighty best of gods with a horse's head, what did Brahma do?"}},{"n":6,"text":"एतन्नः संशयं ब्रह्मन्पुराणज्ञानसंभवम् ।\nकथयस्वोत्तममते महापुरुषनिर्मितम् ।\nपाविताः स्म त्वया ब्रह्मन्पुण्यां कथयता कथाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, of excellent mind, tell us this doubt of ours that arises from Puranic knowledge, about what the Great Person made. You purify us, brahmin, by telling this holy tale."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"कथयिष्यामि ते सर्वं पुराणं वेदसंमितम् ।\nजगौ यद्भगवान्व्यासो राज्ञो धर्मसुतस्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell you the whole ancient account, equal to the Veda, that the blessed Vyasa sang to the king, Dharma's son."}},{"n":8,"text":"श्रुत्वाश्वशिरसो मूर्तिं देवस्य हरिमेधसः ।\nउत्पन्नसंशयो राजा तमेव समचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard of the form of the god with the horse's head, whose wisdom is Hari's, the king grew doubtful and questioned Vyasa about it."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"यत्तद्दर्शितवान्ब्रह्मा देवं हयशिरोधरम् ।\nकिमर्थं तत्समभवद्वपुर्देवोपकल्पितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That god with the horse's head, whom Brahma showed: why did this body, fashioned by the god, come about?"}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"यत्किंचिदिह लोके वै देहबद्धं विशां पते ।\nसर्वं पञ्चभिराविष्टं भूतैरीश्वरबुद्धिजैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, everything in this world that is bound to a body is pervaded by the five elements, born of the Lord's intellect."}},{"n":11,"text":"ईश्वरो हि जगत्स्रष्टा प्रभुर्नारायणो विराट् ।\nभूतान्तरात्मा वरदः सगुणो निर्गुणोऽपि च ।\nभूतप्रलयमव्यक्तं शृणुष्व नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Lord, creator of the universe, the master Narayana, the cosmic Virat, inner self of beings, giver of boons, with qualities and also without, now hear, best of kings, of the dissolution of beings into the unmanifest."}},{"n":12,"text":"धरण्यामथ लीनायामप्सु चैकार्णवे पुरा ।\nज्योतिर्भूते जले चापि लीने ज्योतिषि चानिले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, when the earth had dissolved into the waters, which were one ocean, when the water had become light, and the light dissolved into wind,"}},{"n":13,"text":"वायौ चाकाशसंलीने आकाशे च मनोनुगे ।\nव्यक्ते मनसि संलीने व्यक्ते चाव्यक्ततां गते ॥","meaning":{"en":"when wind dissolved into space, space followed mind, the manifest dissolved into mind, and the manifest became unmanifest,"}},{"n":14,"text":"अव्यक्ते पुरुषं याते पुंसि सर्वगतेऽपि च ।\nतम एवाभवत्सर्वं न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"when the unmanifest went to the Person and the all-pervading Person remained, there was only darkness, and nothing could be known."}},{"n":15,"text":"तमसो ब्रह्म संभूतं तमोमूलमृतात्मकम् ।\nतद्विश्वभावसंज्ञान्तं पौरुषीं तनुमास्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From darkness Brahman arose, rooted in darkness and of the nature of truth, bearing the name that ends the existence of the universe; it took the body of a Person."}},{"n":16,"text":"सोऽनिरुद्ध इति प्रोक्तस्तत्प्रधानं प्रचक्षते ।\nतदव्यक्तमिति ज्ञेयं त्रिगुणं नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is called Aniruddha, and they call that the Pradhana. Know that unmanifest as having three qualities, best of kings."}},{"n":17,"text":"विद्यासहायवान्देवो विष्वक्सेनो हरिः प्रभुः ।\nअप्स्वेव शयनं चक्रे निद्रायोगमुपागतः ।\nजगतश्चिन्तयन्सृष्टिं चित्रां बहुगुणोद्भवाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The god Vishvaksena, Hari, with knowledge as his companion, took his rest on the waters themselves, entering the yoga of sleep, pondering the creation of the world, varied and born of many qualities."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्य चिन्तयतः सृष्टिं महानात्मगुणः स्मृतः ।\nअहंकारस्ततो जातो ब्रह्मा शुभचतुर्मुखः ।\nहिरण्यगर्भो भगवान्सर्वलोकपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he thought of creation, the great self-quality is remembered; from it arose egoity, and Brahma of the four auspicious faces, Hiranyagarbha, the blessed grandfather of all worlds."}},{"n":19,"text":"पद्मेऽनिरुद्धात्संभूतस्तदा पद्मनिभेक्षणः ।\nसहस्रपत्रे द्युतिमानुपविष्टः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born from Aniruddha in a lotus, lotus-eyed, he, the radiant eternal one, sat down on the thousand-petaled flower."}},{"n":20,"text":"ददृशेऽद्भुतसंकाशे लोकानापोमयान्प्रभुः ।\nसत्त्वस्थः परमेष्ठी स ततो भूतगणान्सृजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord saw the worlds, made of water, wondrous in look; established in goodness, Parameshthin then created the hosts of beings."}},{"n":21,"text":"पूर्वमेव च पद्मस्य पत्रे सूर्यांशुसप्रभे ।\nनारायणकृतौ बिन्दू अपामास्तां गुणोत्तरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before this, on the lotus petal gleaming like the sun's rays, two drops of water, made by Narayana and surpassing in quality, had formed."}},{"n":22,"text":"तावपश्यत्स भगवाननादिनिधनोऽच्युतः ।\nएकस्तत्राभवद्बिन्दुर्मध्वाभो रुचिरप्रभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed imperishable one, without beginning or end, saw them. One of the drops was like honey, of lovely sheen."}},{"n":23,"text":"स तामसो मधुर्जातस्तदा नारायणाज्ञया ।\nकठिनस्त्वपरो बिन्दुः कैटभो राजसस्तु सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By Narayana's command that drop became Madhu, of the quality of darkness; the other drop, hard, became Kaitabha, of the quality of passion."}},{"n":24,"text":"तावभ्यधावतां श्रेष्ठौ तमोरजगुणान्वितौ ।\nबलवन्तौ गदाहस्तौ पद्मनालानुसारिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two, best of the mighty, with darkness and passion as their qualities, club in hand, ran forward following the lotus stalk."}},{"n":25,"text":"ददृशातेऽरविन्दस्थं ब्रह्माणममितप्रभम् ।\nसृजन्तं प्रथमं वेदांश्चतुरश्चारुविग्रहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They saw the boundless-radiant Brahma seated on the lotus, creating first the four Vedas of lovely form."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततो विग्रहवन्तौ तौ वेदान्दृष्ट्वासुरोत्तमौ ।\nसहसा जगृहतुर्वेदान्ब्रह्मणः पश्यतस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Vedas embodied, those two best of asuras suddenly seized them while Brahma watched."}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ तौ दानवश्रेष्ठौ वेदान्गृह्य सनातनान् ।\nरसां विविशतुस्तूर्णमुदक्पूर्वे महोदधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two best of danavas, taking the eternal Vedas, quickly entered the nether world, in the great ocean to the north-east."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो हृतेषु वेदेषु ब्रह्मा कश्मलमाविशत् ।\nततो वचनमीशानं प्राह वेदैर्विनाकृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Vedas were stolen, Brahma fell into bewilderment, and, deprived of the Vedas, spoke to the Lord."}},{"n":29,"text":"वेदा मे परमं चक्षुर्वेदा मे परमं बलम् ।\nवेदा मे परमं धाम वेदा मे ब्रह्म चोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Vedas are my supreme eye, the Vedas my supreme strength, the Vedas my supreme abode, and the Vedas my highest Brahman."}},{"n":30,"text":"मम वेदा हृताः सर्वे दानवाभ्यां बलादितः ।\nअन्धकारा हि मे लोका जाता वेदैर्विनाकृताः ।\nवेदानृते हि किं कुर्यां लोकान्वै स्रष्टुमुद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All my Vedas have been taken by force by two danavas. Without the Vedas my worlds have become dark. Without the Vedas, what can I do, when I am about to create the worlds?"}},{"n":31,"text":"अहो बत महद्दुःखं वेदनाशनजं मम ।\nप्राप्तं दुनोति हृदयं तीव्रशोकाय रन्धयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alas, a great grief has come to me from the loss of the Vedas; it torments my heart and cuts me to sharp sorrow."}},{"n":32,"text":"को हि शोकार्णवे मग्नं मामितोऽद्य समुद्धरेत् ।\nवेदांस्तानानयेन्नष्टान्कस्य चाहं प्रियो भवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who could pull me out of this sea of sorrow today and bring back the lost Vedas? And to whom would I be dear?\""}},{"n":33,"text":"इत्येवं भाषमाणस्य ब्रह्मणो नृपसत्तम ।\nहरेः स्तोत्रार्थमुद्भूता बुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतां वर ।\nततो जगौ परं जप्यं साञ्जलिप्रग्रहः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Brahma spoke thus, best of kings, the thought arose in him to praise Hari. Then the lord, hands folded, recited the supreme prayer."}},{"n":34,"text":"नमस्ते ब्रह्महृदय नमस्ते मम पूर्वज ।\nलोकाद्य भुवनश्रेष्ठ सांख्ययोगनिधे विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Homage to you, heart of Brahman; homage to you, my elder; first of the worlds, best of beings, treasury of Samkhya and yoga, all-pervading lord!"}},{"n":35,"text":"व्यक्ताव्यक्तकराचिन्त्य क्षेमं पन्थानमास्थित ।\nविश्वभुक्सर्वभूतानामन्तरात्मन्नयोनिज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maker of the manifest and unmanifest, inconceivable one, established on the path of safety, enjoyer of the universe, inner self of all beings, unborn of any womb!"}},{"n":36,"text":"अहं प्रसादजस्तुभ्यं लोकधाम्ने स्वयंभुवे ।\nत्वत्तो मे मानसं जन्म प्रथमं द्विजपूजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am born of your grace, self-existent one, abode of the worlds; from you came my first, mind-born birth, honored by brahmins."}},{"n":37,"text":"चाक्षुषं वै द्वितीयं मे जन्म चासीत्पुरातनम् ।\nत्वत्प्रसादाच्च मे जन्म तृतीयं वाचिकं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My second birth, the ancient one, was from the eye; by your grace my third, great birth was from speech."}},{"n":38,"text":"त्वत्तः श्रवणजं चापि चतुर्थं जन्म मे विभो ।\nनासिक्यं चापि मे जन्म त्वत्तः पञ्चममुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"My fourth birth, lord, was from hearing, from you; and my fifth birth is said to be from the nose, from you."}},{"n":39,"text":"अण्डजं चापि मे जन्म त्वत्तः षष्ठं विनिर्मितम् ।\nइदं च सप्तमं जन्म पद्मजं मेऽमितप्रभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"My sixth birth, from the egg, was made by you; and this seventh birth of mine, boundless splendor, is from the lotus."}},{"n":40,"text":"सर्गे सर्गे ह्यहं पुत्रस्तव त्रिगुणवर्जितः ।\nप्रथितः पुण्डरीकाक्ष प्रधानगुणकल्पितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In creation after creation I am your son, free of the three qualities, lotus-eyed one, known and designated by the primary qualities."}},{"n":41,"text":"त्वमीश्वरस्वभावश्च स्वयंभूः पुरुषोत्तमः ।\nत्वया विनिर्मितोऽहं वै वेदचक्षुर्वयोतिगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are of the nature of the Lord, self-existent, the Supreme Person; I was made by you, with the Veda as my eye, and I am beyond age."}},{"n":42,"text":"ते मे वेदा हृताश्चक्षुरन्धो जातोऽस्मि जागृहि ।\nददस्व चक्षुषी मह्यं प्रियोऽहं ते प्रियोऽसि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those Vedas of mine have been stolen; I have become blind of eye. Awake! Give me eyes; I am dear to you and you are dear to me.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"एवं स्तुतः स भगवान्पुरुषः सर्वतोमुखः ।\nजहौ निद्रामथ तदा वेदकार्यार्थमुद्यतः ।\nऐश्वरेण प्रयोगेण द्वितीयां तनुमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus praised, the blessed Person who faces every way left sleep, and, ready to act for the Vedas, took a second body by the Lord's power."}},{"n":44,"text":"सुनासिकेन कायेन भूत्वा चन्द्रप्रभस्तदा ।\nकृत्वा हयशिरः शुभ्रं वेदानामालयं प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a body of fair nose, shining like the moon, the lord made a bright horse's head, the abode of the Vedas."}},{"n":45,"text":"तस्य मूर्धा समभवद्द्यौः सनक्षत्रतारका ।\nकेशाश्चास्याभवन्दीर्घा रवेरंशुसमप्रभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His head became the sky with its stars and constellations; his long hair shone like the sun's rays."}},{"n":46,"text":"कर्णावाकाशपाताले ललाटं भूतधारिणी ।\nगङ्गा सरस्वती पुण्या भ्रुवावास्तां महानदी ॥","meaning":{"en":"His ears were the sky and the nether world, his forehead the earth that bears beings; Ganga and holy Sarasvati, the great river, were his two brows."}},{"n":47,"text":"चक्षुषी सोमसूर्यौ ते नासा संध्या पुनः स्मृता ।\nओंकारस्त्वथ संस्कारो विद्युज्जिह्वा च निर्मिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"His eyes were the moon and sun, his nose was the twilight; the syllable Om and its sacramental form, and lightning, were made his tongue."}},{"n":48,"text":"दन्ताश्च पितरो राजन्सोमपा इति विश्रुताः ।\nगोलोको ब्रह्मलोकश्च ओष्ठावास्तां महात्मनः ।\nग्रीवा चास्याभवद्राजन्कालरात्रिर्गुणोत्तरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, his teeth were the ancestors, famed as soma-drinkers; his two lips were Goloka and Brahmaloka; his neck, king, was Kalaratri, surpassing in qualities."}},{"n":49,"text":"एतद्धयशिरः कृत्वा नानामूर्तिभिरावृतम् ।\nअन्तर्दधे स विश्वेशो विवेश च रसां प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made this horse-head, clothed in many forms, the lord of the universe vanished and entered the nether world."}},{"n":50,"text":"रसां पुनः प्रविष्टश्च योगं परममास्थितः ।\nशैक्षं स्वरं समास्थाय ओमिति प्रासृजत्स्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having entered the nether world again, and resting in supreme yoga, he took the voice of a student's recitation and uttered the sound Om."}},{"n":51,"text":"स स्वरः सानुनादी च सर्वगः स्निग्ध एव च ।\nबभूवान्तर्महीभूतः सर्वभूतगुणोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sound was resonant, pervading all, smooth, and, resting within the earth, rose with the qualities of all beings."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततस्तावसुरौ कृत्वा वेदान्समयबन्धनान् ।\nरसातले विनिक्षिप्य यतः शब्दस्ततो द्रुतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two asuras, having bound the Vedas by an agreement and thrown them into the nether world, rushed off toward where the sound was."}},{"n":53,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे राजन्देवो हयशिरोधरः ।\nजग्राह वेदानखिलान्रसातलगतान्हरिः ।\nप्रादाच्च ब्रह्मणे भूयस्ततः स्वां प्रकृतिं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meanwhile, king, the god Hari with the horse's head took all the Vedas that had gone to the nether world, gave them again to Brahma, and then went back to his own nature."}},{"n":54,"text":"स्थापयित्वा हयशिर उदक्पूर्वे महोदधौ ।\nवेदानामालयश्चापि बभूवाश्वशिरास्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He set the horse's head in the great ocean in the north-east, and the Horse-head became the abode of the Vedas."}},{"n":55,"text":"अथ किंचिदपश्यन्तौ दानवौ मधुकैटभौ ।\nपुनराजग्मतुस्तत्र वेगितौ पश्यतां च तौ ।\nयत्र वेदा विनिक्षिप्तास्तत्स्थानं शून्यमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the danavas Madhu and Kaitabha, seeing nothing, hurried back there; where the Vedas had been thrown, the place was empty."}},{"n":56,"text":"तत उत्तममास्थाय वेगं बलवतां वरौ ।\nपुनरुत्तस्थतुः शीघ्रं रसानामालयात्तदा ।\nददृशाते च पुरुषं तमेवादिकरं प्रभुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two best of the mighty rose swiftly again from the abode of the nether world with the highest speed, and saw the same Person, the original maker, the lord,"}},{"n":57,"text":"श्वेतं चन्द्रविशुद्धाभमनिरुद्धतनौ स्थितम् ।\nभूयोऽप्यमितविक्रान्तं निद्रायोगमुपागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"white, pure as the moon, resting in the body of Aniruddha, of boundless prowess, again entered into the yoga of sleep,"}},{"n":58,"text":"आत्मप्रमाणरचिते अपामुपरि कल्पिते ।\nशयने नागभोगाढ्ये ज्वालामालासमावृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"on a bed made to his own size, set above the waters, rich with serpent coils and encircled by garlands of flame,"}},{"n":59,"text":"निष्कल्मषेण सत्त्वेन संपन्नं रुचिरप्रभम् ।\nतं दृष्ट्वा दानवेन्द्रौ तौ महाहासममुञ्चताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"endowed with stainless goodness and lovely radiance. Seeing him, the two lords of danavas gave a great laugh."}},{"n":60,"text":"ऊचतुश्च समाविष्टौ रजसा तमसा च तौ ।\nअयं स पुरुषः श्वेतः शेते निद्रामुपागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Possessed by passion and darkness, they said: \"This white Person lies asleep."}},{"n":61,"text":"अनेन नूनं वेदानां कृतमाहरणं रसात् ।\nकस्यैष को नु खल्वेष किं च स्वपिति भोगवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely he took the Vedas from the nether world. Whose is he, who is he, and why does he sleep, coiled?\""}},{"n":62,"text":"इत्युच्चारितवाक्यौ तौ बोधयामासतुर्हरिम् ।\nयुद्धार्थिनौ तु विज्ञाय विबुद्धः पुरुषोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying so, they woke Hari. Knowing they wanted battle, the Supreme Person awoke,"}},{"n":63,"text":"निरीक्ष्य चासुरेन्द्रौ तौ ततो युद्धे मनो दधे ।\nअथ युद्धं समभवत्तयोर्नारायणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"looked at those two lords of asuras, and set his mind on fighting. Then a battle took place between them and Narayana."}},{"n":64,"text":"रजस्तमोविष्टतनू तावुभौ मधुकैटभौ ।\nब्रह्मणोपचितिं कुर्वञ्जघान मधुसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhu and Kaitabha, both with bodies filled with passion and darkness, were killed by Madhusudana, who did it as an offering of honor to Brahma."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततस्तयोर्वधेनाशु वेदापहरणेन च ।\nशोकापनयनं चक्रे ब्रह्मणः पुरुषोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, by killing them and recovering the Vedas, the Supreme Person removed Brahma's grief."}},{"n":66,"text":"ततः परिवृतो ब्रह्मा हतारिर्वेदसत्कृतः ।\nनिर्ममे स तदा लोकान्कृत्स्नान्स्थावरजङ्गमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brahma, surrounded, his enemies slain, honored by the Vedas, created all the worlds, moving and unmoving."}},{"n":67,"text":"दत्त्वा पितामहायाग्र्यां बुद्धिं लोकविसर्गिकीम् ।\nतत्रैवान्तर्दधे देवो यत एवागतो हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given the grandfather the excellent intellect for emitting the worlds, the god Hari vanished right there, from where he had come."}},{"n":68,"text":"तौ दानवौ हरिर्हत्वा कृत्वा हयशिरस्तनुम् ।\nपुनः प्रवृत्तिधर्मार्थं तामेव विदधे तनुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed those two danavas and assumed the horse-headed body, Hari again assumed that same body for the sake of the dharma of activity."}},{"n":69,"text":"एवमेष महाभागो बभूवाश्वशिरा हरिः ।\nपौराणमेतदाख्यातं रूपं वरदमैश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the greatly fortunate Hari became Horse-headed. This ancient, boon-giving, sovereign form has been told."}},{"n":70,"text":"यो ह्येतद्ब्राह्मणो नित्यं शृणुयाद्धारयेत वा ।\nन तस्याध्ययनं नाशमुपगच्छेत्कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin who always hears or retains this will never lose his study."}},{"n":71,"text":"आराध्य तपसोग्रेण देवं हयशिरोधरम् ।\nपाञ्चालेन क्रमः प्राप्तो रामेण पथि देशिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having propitiated the god with the horse's head through fierce austerity, the Panchala obtained the Krama, on the path Rama showed."}},{"n":72,"text":"एतद्धयशिरो राजन्नाख्यानं तव कीर्तितम् ।\nपुराणं वेदसमितं यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I have told you this Horse-head account, the ancient tale equal to the Veda, that you asked me about."}},{"n":73,"text":"यां यामिच्छेत्तनुं देवः कर्तुं कार्यविधौ क्वचित् ।\nतां तां कुर्याद्विकुर्वाणः स्वयमात्मानमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever body the god wishes to take for a given task, he creates it by changing himself, himself through himself."}},{"n":74,"text":"एष वेदनिधिः श्रीमानेष वै तपसो निधिः ।\nएष योगश्च सांख्यं च ब्रह्म चाग्र्यं हरिर्विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the treasury of the Vedas, glorious, a treasury of austerity; he is yoga, Samkhya, and the supreme Brahman, the all-pervading Hari."}},{"n":75,"text":"नारायणपरा वेदा यज्ञा नारायणात्मकाः ।\nतपो नारायणपरं नारायणपरा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vedas have Narayana as their aim, sacrifices are of Narayana's nature, austerity has Narayana as its aim, and Narayana is the supreme destination."}},{"n":76,"text":"नारायणपरं सत्यमृतं नारायणात्मकम् ।\nनारायणपरो धर्मः पुनरावृत्तिदुर्लभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Truth has Narayana as its aim, and order is of Narayana's nature; dharma has Narayana as its aim, from which return is hard to find."}},{"n":77,"text":"प्रवृत्तिलक्षणश्चैव धर्मो नारायणात्मकः ।\nनारायणात्मको गन्धो भूमौ श्रेष्ठतमः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dharma marked by activity is also of Narayana's nature; smell, the best quality on earth, is said to be of Narayana's nature."}},{"n":78,"text":"अपां चैव गुणो राजन्रसो नारायणात्मकः ।\nज्योतिषां च गुणो रूपं स्मृतं नारायणात्मकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, taste, the quality of waters, is of Narayana's nature, and form, the quality of lights, is said to be of Narayana's nature."}},{"n":79,"text":"नारायणात्मकश्चापि स्पर्शो वायुगुणः स्मृतः ।\nनारायणात्मकश्चापि शब्द आकाशसंभवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touch, the quality of wind, is said to be of Narayana's nature, and sound, born of space, is also of Narayana's nature."}},{"n":80,"text":"मनश्चापि ततो भूतमव्यक्तगुणलक्षणम् ।\nनारायणपरः कालो ज्योतिषामयनं च यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mind too is an element, marked by the unmanifest quality. Time, and the course of the luminaries, have Narayana as their aim."}},{"n":81,"text":"नारायणपरा कीर्तिः श्रीश्च लक्ष्मीश्च देवताः ।\nनारायणपरं सांख्यं योगो नारायणात्मकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fame, Shri, Lakshmi, and the goddesses have Narayana as their aim; Samkhya has Narayana as its aim, and yoga is of Narayana's nature."}},{"n":82,"text":"कारणं पुरुषो येषां प्रधानं चापि कारणम् ।\nस्वभावश्चैव कर्माणि दैवं येषां च कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who take the Person as the cause, for those for whom the Pradhana is the cause, for those for whom nature, actions, or fate are the cause,"}},{"n":83,"text":"पञ्चकारणसंख्यातो निष्ठा सर्वत्र वै हरिः ।\nतत्त्वं जिज्ञासमानानां हेतुभिः सर्वतोमुखैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the doctrine is counted as five causes, and for those who seek the truth by reasons in every direction, Hari is the ground everywhere."}},{"n":84,"text":"तत्त्वमेको महायोगी हरिर्नारायणः प्रभुः ।\nसब्रह्मकानां लोकानामृषीणां च महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hari Narayana, the lord, the great yogi, alone is the truth for the worlds with Brahma and for the great sages."}},{"n":85,"text":"सांख्यानां योगिनां चापि यतीनामात्मवेदिनाम् ।\nमनीषितं विजानाति केशवो न तु तस्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava knows what is thought by Samkhyas, yogis, ascetics, and knowers of the self, but they do not know his."}},{"n":86,"text":"ये केचित्सर्वलोकेषु दैवं पित्र्यं च कुर्वते ।\nदानानि च प्रयच्छन्ति तप्यन्ति च तपो महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever people in all worlds perform for the gods and ancestors, whatever gifts they give and great austerity they practice,"}},{"n":87,"text":"सर्वेषामाश्रयो विष्णुरैश्वरं विधिमास्थितः ।\nसर्वभूतकृतावासो वासुदेवेति चोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishnu, following the Lord's rule, is the refuge of all; he is called Vasudeva, for he has made his dwelling in all beings."}},{"n":88,"text":"अयं हि नित्यः परमो महर्षि-\nर्महाविभूतिर्गुणवान्निर्गुणाख्यः ।\nगुणैश्च संयोगमुपैति शीघ्रं\nकालो यथर्तावृतुसंप्रयुक्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This one, the eternal, supreme great sage of great glory, with qualities yet called without qualities, quickly comes into contact with the qualities, as Time joins with each season in turn."}},{"n":89,"text":"नैवास्य विन्दन्ति गतिं महात्मनो\nन चागतिं कश्चिदिहानुपश्यति ।\nज्ञानात्मकाः संयमिनो महर्षयः\nपश्यन्ति नित्यं पुरुषं गुणाधिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled one's course is never found, nor does anyone here see his coming; the great sages, self-controlled and of the nature of knowledge, always see the Person who surpasses the qualities."}}]}]}